OP_IRQ_SET with IRQ_SET_PERIOD on a line that fired more than a period ago
counts one period from its deadline and no further,
so a thread that woke late arms a deadline the clock has already passed.
The timer fires every due timer line,
so an Irq armed on one has its deadline ahead of the count.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: armed timer line is due
Witness: fuzz timer-period-skips

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -929,7 +929,7 @@ static uint32_t timer_period(struct irq *irq, uint64_t period)
     uint64_t now = timer_now(), rest;
     if (irq_due(irq, now)) {
         uint64_t skipped = timer_periods(now - irq->deadline, period, &rest);
-        irq->deadline = now + period - rest;
+        irq->deadline += period;
         return skipped > UINT32_MAX ? UINT32_MAX : (uint32_t)skipped;
     }
     timer_periods(irq->deadline - now - 1, period, &rest);
